BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (An exFAT volume has a main boot region, backup boot region, FAT region and data region with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (a cluster heap. The main boot sector records partition offset, volume length, FAT offset) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (and length, cluster heap offset and count, root directory first cluster, revision, flags) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (and sector/cluster shifts. The boot region includes a checksum; the backup helps retain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (boot metadata after certain failures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (The cluster heap stores the root directory, allocation bitmap, uppercase conversion table,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (subdirectories and file content. The first data cluster is numbered two. Cluster index) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (entries are 32 bits, but the bitmap rather than the FAT is authoritative for which clusters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (are allocated. Directory entry sets combine primary File entries with Stream Extension and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 512.0 Tm (File Name secondary entries.) Tj ET
