BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (Allocation bitmap bits indicate used and free clusters. A file may be represented as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (contiguous extent without needing a per-cluster FAT chain when the NoFatChain flag applies;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (fragmented files use the FAT to follow linked clusters. This is a major difference from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (classic FAT12/16/32 and avoids much table access for contiguous files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 597.0 Tm (Directories consist of 32-byte records combined into validated entry sets with secondary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (counts and set checksums. Filenames use UTF-16 code units and a volume upcase table for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (case-insensitive lookup. The stream extension records the first cluster, data length and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (valid-data length. Unknown critical entries must not be ignored as though they were benign) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (extensions.) Tj ET
