BT /F2 16 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (DESIGN TRADE-OFFS AND HISTORICAL LIMITATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (exFAT supports 64-bit file lengths and much larger clusters than the original FAT variants,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (and its allocation bitmap decouples free-space tracking from chain traversal. Larger) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (permissible clusters improve scalability but also increase possible internal fragmentation;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (the chosen geometry must respect device and interoperability limits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 597.0 Tm (The format avoids the complexity of a tree-indexed or pooled copy-on-write filesystem,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (favouring portable storage. It does not inherently provide Unix ACL semantics,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (filesystem-wide snapshots or cryptographic end-to-end checksums. Filesystem consistency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (under abrupt removal remains a responsibility of implementation write ordering and repair) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (utilities.) Tj ET
